# Client sites under `sites/` are a fork-level addition upstream does not have, so the root
# `lint:css` — which is the framework's lint — had never been pointed at one until upstream wired
# every always-running check into CI (spec 091). It then reported 4870 errors on Perego's authored
# `perego-theme/style.css`, none of them about the framework.
#
# Same call as `jest.config.js` makes for the same reason: root tooling covers the framework, each
# client site carries its own. Perego's does not have a stylelint setup yet, so this ignore is a
# deliberate gap rather than a solved problem — the CSS is unlinted until that lands, and reordering
# it to satisfy `no-descending-specificity` would need a full visual re-verification anyway.
sites/**

# The raw design handoff is git-ignored reference material, so CI never sees it and only a local run
# ever hits it — 3746 errors from a vendor stylesheet nobody here wrote or ships. Listed so `npm run
# lint:css` means the same thing on this machine as it does in CI; a local-only failure that CI
# cannot reproduce is the fastest way to teach someone to stop reading the output.
_design_handoff/**
